<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36772" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξανδρᾰποδ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>reduce to utter slavery,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθήνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.94
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.1.15
			</span></i>:—mostly in 
				Med.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξανδρᾰποδ-ίζομαι</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς Τεγεήτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.66
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.2.16
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν τεθνεώτων ἐ. τοὺς
				βίους</span>
			<i>confiscate</i> the substance of the deceased, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				32.5.11
			</span></i>.—The 
				Att.
			
			fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξανδραποδιοῦμαι,</span>
			
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιεῦμαι,</span> which is mostly trans. (as
			in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.66
			</span></i>), takes a pass. sense in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.9
			</span></i>: so aor. 1
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξηνδραποδίσθην</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				108
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				50.4
			</span></i>: pf.
			part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξηνδραποδισμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Cal.</u>
				19
			</span></i>.</div>
